BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:nyc-20261023-28@tonight
DTSTAMP:20261019T195625Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261023T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261023T210000
SUMMARY:Curtis Stigers
LOCATION:Birdland Theater\, Hell's Kitchen
DESCRIPTION:For the past 30 years\, the singer\, songwriter\, saxophonist a
 
nd guitarist Curtis Stigers has been making records that confound those who
 
 try to categorize his music or put him in a box. Stigers burst onto the re
 
cording scene in 1991 with his eponymously-titled debut album\, which sold 
 
1.5 million copies and spawned several self-penned\, pop/soul hit singles\,
 
 including \, "rdquo" -> You're All That Matters To Me"\, \, "rdquo" -> Nev
 
er Saw A Miracle" and the worldwide top-ten hit\, \, "rdquo" -> I Wonder Wh
 
y." The next year the singer/songwriter/saxophonist recorded Nick Lowe's \,
 
 "rdquo" -> (What's So Funny 'Bout) Peace Love and Understanding" for \, "r
 
dquo" -> The Bodyguard" soundtrack\, which has sold over 45 million copies 
 
worldwide. Stigers recorded two more pop-oriented albums in the 1990s and m
 
ade guest appearances on several albums\, including two by his early musica
 
l mentor\, the legendary jazz pianist Gene Harris. In 2001 Stigers pivoted 
 
artistically and signed with Concord Jazz. Over the next 18 years he record
 
ed nine genre-busting albums\, combining his jazz sensibilities with his lo
 
ve for emotional\, well-written modern songs from a wide variety of sources
 
 including rock\, blues\, soul\, country and folk. During this period Stige
 
rs co-wrote and sang \, "rdquo" -> This Life"\, the Emmy Award-nominated th
 
eme song to the wildly popular TV show \, "rdquo" -> Sons Of Anarchy"\, and
 
 also made cameo appearances in the Seth MacFarlane movies \, "rdquo" -> Te
 
d" and \, "rdquo" -> Ted 2". All the while\, Stigers was cultivating a succ
 
essful and enduring touring career\, playing concerts around the world\, pe
 
rforming songs from his jazz albums as well as newly reconstructed \, "rdqu
 
o" -> jazz" versions of his hit songs from his early pop albums. Tickets & 
 
info: https://www.ticketweb.com/event/curtis-stigers-birdland-theater-ticke
 
ts/15005073
URL:https://www.ticketweb.com/event/curtis-stigers-birdland-theater-tickets
 
/15005073
END:VEVENT
